title ALES125 — Lotus's stereo_reverse: turning a master end for end, both channels in lockstep, total (no refusal)
prompt Continue the recurring baton (prin recur) on the ALES/Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think Sixth lap of the session's recur run. The stereo edit family has carried every span-edit and the grid nudge; the crux now is to open the stereo suite's pure-rearrangement class (every position changes, no value), and reverse (ALES104) is its plainest member — the Reverse menu item, the reversed cymbal swell.
think Read reverse.rye (mono, void, total, length holds; len/2 swaps from both ends inward, middle sample its own mirror). Like shift, the lift runs mono reverse per channel with no argument; total and length-holding, so balance is preserved trivially and no fault forwards.
think Wrote the design read, module (void, no try), witness. Four laws proven on metal: stereo reverse law (each channel == ALES104 byte for byte, sample i holds len-1-i), balance/length law (left.len == right.len even and odd, both hold length), involution law (twice is the identity on both channels), permutation/fixpoint law (each channel's peak through ALES13 unchanged, empty/single/palindrome pairs their own reverse).
obs This opens the rearrangement class with the involution keystone — a mistaken reverse reverses back to the byte on both speakers. invert (ALES105, value-mirror), rotate (ALES106), and nyquist_flip (ALES107) are the natural next three lifts to complete the class. Witness GREEN first run; tame_style_check clean.
loom witness=ales_stereo_reverse_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2
file lotus/stereo_reverse.rye ALES125 — stereo_reverse lifts ALES104's total mono reverse to a StereoClip, no validation needed, four laws.
file tools/ales_stereo_reverse_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-reverse line.
